  "id": "COMPOUND:3534 - PROTEIN:1157",
  "verbalization": "Radicicol is implicated in the regulation of Platelet glycoprotein IX through a multi-step mechanism involving the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C. This receptor is targeted by two compounds, Monotiporic Acid B and Stagonolide F, both of which are known to interact with Platelet glycoprotein IX. The evidence suggests that Radicicol acts as a modulator of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, which in turn influences the activity of Platelet glycoprotein IX. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and plausible pathway, with each step linking Radicicol to the receptor and then to the target protein. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Radicicol may exert its effects on Platelet glycoprotein IX through the activation or inhibition of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, potentially altering the function of the glycoprotein in platelet aggregation or other related processes. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple compounds that target the same receptor and ultimately the same protein, suggesting a potential role for Radicicol in modulating platelet function through this pathway.",
